  "paper_id": "ccs-2025-megablocks-breaking-the-logarithmic-i-o-overhead-barrier-9d3c6c59",
  "title": "MegaBlocks: Breaking the Logarithmic I/O-Overhead Barrier for Oblivious RAM",
  "abstract": "Oblivious RAM (ORAM) is a central cryptographic primitive that enables secure memory access while hiding access patterns. Among existing ORAM paradigms, hierarchical ORAMs were long considered impractical despite their asymptotic optimality. However, recent advancements (FutORAMa, CCS'23) demonstrate that hierarchical ORAM-based schemes can be made efficient given sufficient client-side memory. In this work, we present a new hierarchical ORAM construction that achieves practical performance without requiring large local memory.",
